    <statement><tabular valign="top">
<row>
<cell>Match each double integral in polar with the graph 
of the region of integration.
<ol>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{3\pi/2}^{2\pi} \int_{0}^{2} f(r,\theta) \, r \, dr \, d\theta</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle  \int_{1}^{2} \int_{3\pi/4}^{7\pi/4} f(r,\theta) \, r  \, d\theta \, dr</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{1} \int_{0}^{3\pi/4} f(r,\theta) \, r \, d\theta \, dr</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{-\pi/4}^{3\pi/4} \int_{1}^{2} f(r,\theta) \, r \, dr \, d\theta</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2\pi} \int_{0}^{1} f(r,\theta) \, r \, dr \, d\theta</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{0}^{2\pi} \int_{1}^{2} f(r,\theta) \, r \, dr \, d\theta</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle \int_{3\pi/4}^{3\pi/2} \int_{0}^{1} f(r,\theta) \, r \, dr \, d\theta</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>\displaystyle  \int_{0}^{1} \int_{-\pi/2}^{3\pi/4} f(r,\theta) \, r  \, d\theta \, dr</m>
</li>
</ol></cell>
